# Agentic Dev Toolkit

This repository ships the Cursor plugin Agentic Dev Toolkit (see `.cursor-plugin/plugin.json`).

## Skills — read before acting

| Trigger | Skill path |
|---|---|
| Design SoT / mockup access (Figma, FigCraft, …) | `skills/design-source-access/SKILL.md` |
| FigCraft maquette edit / designer↔dev | `skills/figcraft-designer-dev/SKILL.md` |
| FigCraft comments (G1) | `skills/figcraft-comments/SKILL.md` |
| Any visual UI change | `skills/visual-quality-gate/SKILL.md` |
| Lint/format/typecheck/tests for this project | `skills/code-quality/SKILL.md` |
| Before Done / merge | `skills/verify-handoff/SKILL.md` |
| Need a project verify CLI (not disposable bash) | `skills/create-verify-cli/SKILL.md` |
| Any automation need | `skills/no-disposable-scripts/SKILL.md` |
| Measuring task signals / model routing data | `skills/code-metrics/SKILL.md` |

Concrete toolchains (exact design product, package manager, linters) come from **conversation or consumer-repo context**. These skills define the process cards; they do not hardcode one stack.

**FigCraft live override:** when context says the owner must see mockup edits immediately, edit via **live collab** (host + file id from context) — not only the versioned `.figcraft`. See `figcraft-designer-dev`.

Paths are relative to this plugin root (or `.cursor-plugin/agentic-dev-toolkit/` when vendored).

## Hard rules

1. **Verify before Done** — run applicable gates; call `bin/verify-checklist`. Fill gate criteria from the stack/design SoT stated in context.
2. **No disposable scripts** — use `bin/` / `tools/` / repo CLI; extend them in-repo instead of `/tmp` bash. Prefer `create-verify-cli` when verify is recurrent.
3. Prefer toolbox bins under this plugin over one-off shell.

## Toolbox entry points

- `bin/verify-checklist` (alias: `tools/verify-checklist`)
- `bin/metrics-append` (alias: `tools/metrics-append`)
- `bin/metrics-summarize` (alias: `tools/metrics-summarize`) — optional before spawn to pick a model from JSONL
